{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/109956-so-what-kith-s-seemings-etc-are-popular-with-your-group","id":109956,"title":"So what Kith's/Seemings/etc are popular with your group?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-10T01:04:03-07:00","id":109956,"title":"So what Kith's/Seemings/etc are popular with your group?","content":"So I was wondering what Kiths, Seemings, Courts, Entitlements or combinations of Kiths are popular with your groups. What do people seem to be playing, or not playing? I'll list what I recently gathered in looking over old game notes.<br /> <br /> In my case, these are collected from four games, two current two from a few years ago. Apparently Changeling games tend to happen in twos around here.<br /> <br /> Courts:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Autumn Court 8<br /> Summer Court 7<br /> Spring Court 6<br /> Winter Court 4<br /> Dawn Court 1<br /> Moon Court 1<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I should note Both non Seasonal Courts are from the same game, though at least in my games all the Courts were options. I think one of the four required Seasonal.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seemings:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Darklings 8<br /> Elementals 7<br /> Beasts 5<br /> Wizened 3<br /> Fairest 2<br /> Ogres 2<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Both Ogres were from the same player. Also most Darklings were from the older two games (5 of 8) while most Elementals are from the more recent ones (5 of 7). I guess people have gotten less goth and more elemental? I dunno.<br /> <br /> I was surprised at the lack of Fairest. Sidhe were rather overwhelmingly popular in my Dreaming games it is...interesting to see Fairest being far less represented.<br /> <br /> Kiths:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Gravewight 3<br /> Manikin 3<br /> Snowskin 3<br /> Whisperwisp 3<br /> Antiquarian 2<br /> Draconic 2 <br /> Leechfinger 2<br /> Razorhand 2<br /> Runnerswift 2<br /> Smith 2<br /> Venombite 2<br /> Windwing 2<br /> Airtouched 1<br /> Chatelaine 1<br /> Chirurgen 1<br /> Coldscale 1<br /> Coyote 1<br /> Cyclopean 1<br /> Drudge 1<br /> Hunterheart 1<br /> Incubus 1<br /> Levinquick 1<br /> Lurker 1<br /> Metalflesh 1<br /> Minstrel 1<br /> Mirrorskin 1<br /> Moonborn 1<br /> Oracle 1<br /> Skitterskulk 1<br /> Stonebones 1<br /> Truefriend 1<br /> Tunnelgrub 1<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not much to add, except that my current game is the first with no Manikins. Also, all the Manikins have been single Kith, while the non-Manikins have all been dual. Also, all three Snowskins have been from recent games.<br /> <br /> Entitlements<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> College of Worms 2<br /> Bishopric of Blackbirds 2<br /> Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches 2<br /> Barony of the Lesser Ones 1<br /> Family of Silent Nights 1<br /> The Lost Pantheon 1<br /> Magistrate of the Wax Mask 1<br /> Magus of Gilded Thorns 1<br /> The Office of the Vizieral Council 1<br /> Order of Oneirophysics 1<br /> The Phantom Tong 1<br /> The Sacred Band of the Golden Standard 1<br /> Scarecrow Ministry 1<br /> Tolltaker Knighthood 1<br /> Twilight Gleaners 1<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Main thing is so far only two games have really had anyone with Entitlements, and both those have nearly every PC having one. Some may get added as my current game they may get some.<br /> <br /> So what are your games like? What are people playing or not playing? Any overwhelming favorites?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T02:50:45-07:00","id":109977,"title":"","content":"I've only run the one Changeling game, which is still ongoing. Thus far, we've had one Autumn Court Elemental with Earthbones and Gargantuan kiths (really, really stupid amounts of health), one Winter Court Darkling with the Mirrorskin Kith, one Summer Court Wizened with the Soldier/Artisan (or something, can't recall the exact name) Dual Kith, one Summer Court Beast with the Runnerswift Kith, and one Spring Court Wizened with the Chirurgeon Kith. The Autumn Court Elemental is the only member to have gained an Entitlement, joining the Lost Pantheon upon reaching Wyrd 6.<br /> <br /> I've also played in another game, where we had a Winter Court Ogre with the Gristlegrinder Kith, a Winter Court Elemental with the Snowskin Kith, a Spring Court Darkling with the Nightsinger Kith, and a Summer Court Beast with the Runnerswift Kith. No Entitlements in that game.<br /> <br /> So, basically, a pretty diverse spread without any obvious favourites. Like you, I was rather surprised to note the total lack of interest in Fairest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T03:16:07-07:00","id":109985,"title":"","content":"With my Changeling LARP which had about 40 people in it, we only had 1 or 2 Darklings and Ogres, the most popular were the Fairest wih Elementals falling a close second. We had surprisingly few Summer Courtiers, from what I remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T04:37:24-07:00","id":110013,"title":"","content":"My most recent campaign had an allience of Spring and Autumn Court Changelings trying to stop a conflict between the Winter and Summer Courts. So folks were Spring or Autumn. We had no Fairest, the Autumns were a Darkling (Nightsong), Wizzened (Chatinlene), Beast(Hunterheart), and the Springs were Elemental (I forget the right terms for a Windspirit and a Forest Spirit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T16:23:31-07:00","id":110387,"title":"","content":"I can't shake the idea that a LARP full of people playing Fairest would be amusing for all sorts of reasons.<br /> <br /> I have not LARPed since the 90s, so my memories of LARP would be &quot;well there are the 8 people not playing Darklings over there...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T20:28:46-07:00","id":111206,"title":"","content":"With all the Changeling games I've ran, Seemings have ran the gamut with some mild leanings towards Fairest, Flora-based Elementals, Darklings, Ogres and Wizened (with Fairest, and Elementals having the most consistent interest). Of all the Seemings Beasts I've never had anyone take an active interest in yet, and it's been some years. I find that strange, but there you go between LARP and Tabletop. They're just getting no love, but I think some of that may be baggage and sour-tastes from folks C:tD days (Pooka, I'm looking at you even as I tell people to utterly forget anything they remember of C:tD in relation to C:tL).<br /> <br /> The Fairest thing is likely some minor residual baggage (again) from C:tD and super-kith Sidhe; drastically unbalanced compared to the rest with the most goodies accessible, and the &quot;Look at me, I'm awesome and I just get more shit&quot; fairy princess crap all rolled neatly into one obnoxious package chock full of Arts and House-related goodies that overshadowed -everyone- by a good stretch. At least now it's far less &quot;They're popular because they're the super-kith&quot; and more &quot;I want to be something regal, beautiful, commanding, frightening and impressive. The Fairest got that in spades built right in&quot;. Being socially strong sure doesn't hurt in games with heavy politics, so I don't begrudge that popular choice especially when I actually rather like the Fairest (and all the Seemings, honestly) and one is using the Social maneuvering systems.<br /> <br /> Kiths have been very spread out. I've encouraged Dual-Kiths/Wyrd Progression so there isn't too heavy reuse of individual Kiths outside of a couple. Oddly enough once again something unexpected; Soldiers have seen interest consistently despite having one of the worst Kith Blessings out there. I think it may be folks overestimating what it does and wanting a bit of martial flair. There's been a heavy lean towards wilds/plant/outdoors Kiths; Farwalkers, Woodbloods, variants of Venomtouched/Blightbents with toxic flora, Flowering, Sleep Scent (modified from the Somnolent Perfume aspect in Autumn Nightmares) etc. but that could well change. There's been some repeated interest in variants of Stonebones as well.<br /> <br /> Entitlements rarely get much interest. Honestly, I rarely find them all that relevant myself unless you're dealing with a very large setting filled to the brim with Lost npcs given how they generally operate; they lose quite a bit of interest factor when there's only a lone representative I find. I've had one Lord Sage of the Unknown Reaches and some initial interest in an Adjucator of the Wheel PC-wise, but not too much else. They're definitely one of those things that I feel make the greatest impact in a very bustling local Freehold that already has very filled out Courts; once people are more invested and interacting with them, -then- they tend to stray into the Entitlements if at all. I'm still hoping someone may go towards the Scarecrow Ministry sometime, and a few PCs really seemed to be going towards being Hedge Wardens.<br /> <br /> PC-wise it has been the Spring Court that has had the most interest along with a nod towards the Night Court and Dusk Court. Winter Court seems to get the least interest overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T22:23:02-07:00","id":111278,"title":"","content":"Your Flora based comment is interesting. Most of our Elementals have been Mannikins...and no Flora based yet. I do see the draw, though, the concept does sound neat.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Dreaming Effect&quot; is interesting to consider...I wonder how groups would go who never played it vs. did, just to see if, say, Pooka or Sidhe were an Influence (I still love Sluagh myself, which has expanded to include Darklings ^_^) And yea, Duel Kiths seem common, and not without reason...it's a useful advantage worth every point and it really gives interesting new dynamics to a character and their story, and seeing what kind of Faerie you can build. I am very happy with it's addition.<br /> <br /> The Court comment seems interesting, just because Spring, Night and Dusk is not a combo I would have expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T22:55:23-07:00","id":111293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/109956-so-what-kith-s-seemings-etc-are-popular-with-your-group?p=110387#post110387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't shake the idea that a LARP full of people playing Fairest would be amusing for all sorts of reasons.<br /> <br /> I have not LARPed since the 90s, so my memories of LARP would be &quot;well there are the 8 people not playing Darklings over there...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It got a bit 'Mean Girls', and it was <i>great</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T01:45:38-07:00","id":111340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/109956-so-what-kith-s-seemings-etc-are-popular-with-your-group?p=111278#post111278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Dreaming Effect&quot; is interesting to consider...I wonder how groups would go who never played it vs. did, just to see if, say, Pooka or Sidhe were an Influence</div> </div> </div> </div>It interests me, too. I can only speak for my sample size of 1,* but Beast and Fairest have actually been the Seemings I've found most appealing, and I've never known anything of C:tD.<br /> <br /> I'm actually kind of curious now. The Sidhe seems easy enough for me, but I haven't heard enough on the Pooka front. I've heard vague, negative comments like those here -- and Holden mentioned that Exalted's Fair Folk 1e outline contained some choice words for Pooka fans, with no elaboration -- but I don't have any context for the reason. Would anyone be willing to enlighten me?<br /> <br /> * Presuming I can even do that, having gotten... not very far into a single PbP game a year or two ago ^_^o On-topic with the thread, we had my Fairest dual-kith Minstrel/Broadback, a Wizened Gameplayer, another Fairest with a Kith I can't remember (Muse?), and a Beast Runnerswift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 04-12-2014, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T02:26:56-07:00","id":111355,"title":"","content":"Pooka are a Kith (like Seemings in CTL) which has the weakness of always needing to lie...they must make a WP roll to tell the truth. They have been typically portrayed as pranksters and a little goofy. Their powers are the ability to turn into an animal when unobserved, and an easy time getting people to open up to them and tell them secrets.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with Pooka in and of themselves. There is no draw for me, but I have seen them played very well. And while many probably even most do play them well, they tend to draw a certain sort of player to them who tends to be very disruptive and and ignore the tone of the game...the same sort who tends to play &quot;fishmalks&quot; and before that, Kender. Thus a lot of people tend to hate Pooka outright, despite the fact they can be played well. At the same time, I can't blame the GM who gets frustrated with a player who seems intent on using their character type as an excuse to mess up other player's play experiences.<br /> <br /> I can't speak about Exalted too much, but I suspect the choice words were about the sort of player who wanted to enter a serious Exalted game, turn people purple, and force people to sing about pants, or something like that.<br /> <br /> There's a line. Some people can be frustrated by Pooka who, unlike say Malkavians, actually have some reason to be fairly comedic with some concepts. I can kick a player whose Malkavian's derangement is apparently to yell &quot;PANTS&quot; at odd times...but Pooka tend to be a little goofy, being representative of childlike whimsy and imagination. A Pooka behaving that way is not necessarily indicative of a bad player...a certain amount of such is right there in the description, and it is systematically hard not to have them lie all the damn time for no reason. Some people don't like that.<br /> <br /> Is that fairly clear?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T03:47:01-07:00","id":111375,"title":"","content":"I could write a long essay on the Pooka and my years of experience with them (including playing one) but I believe Baron covered it more politely. Lets just say... they were something of a watermark on a lot of what many WoD fans found wrong with C:tD. That said, their Kithbook did a -spectacular- job expanding and diversifying them, sometimes to the chagrin some of the prior Pooka fans.<br /> <br /> I'm not too surprised at the Court choices myself (anymore; Spring interest initially caught me off guard). I take a fairly dark tone for their games or when they're included in a mixed chronicle; in a way it makes sense that the Court of Fatalism (and really, living risky, to the Nth degree lifestyles because you're fucked anyhow in the grand scheme of things), the Spring (Desire, living life to the fullest and making a new one) and Night (Disgust, embracing the uglier aspects of ones existence, another sort of &quot;living life without inhibitions&quot; vibe) cropped up as popular choices in the face of that as well as in other chronicles. There is a bit of an underlying common thread in them in hindsight, if not less inhibitions in some ways. It should be no surprise that my newest Changeling player went with a South (and they nearly went Spring); that subext seems to be staying strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T12:33:37-07:00","id":111691,"title":"","content":"That's true, my current game has a Night, and their &quot;Never be ashamed&quot; (with the understanding they are not necessarily amoral, just refused to be ashamed of what they are or do) does mean she gets along well with the Spring Courtier. Thanks for further discussion.<br /> <br /> For those with PCs who don't necessarily only follow the Four main courts, do you have lots of Courts in your freehold, or do some players simply choose to go for them? My current is the first with non seasonals, and one player chose Dawn knowing there were currently no NPCs of that Court, while the Night Courtier went that way partially as all 5 other players were of different Courts and partially because there was a Day and Night Court in neighboring LA, even if the actual setting only has Seasonal Courts beyond an emissary from each Day and Night.<br /> <br /> Also do you (you being those with non-seasonals) make any allowances for their having fewer Contracts? Directionals, Dawn and Dusk get one each and Day and Night don't get any. I have done nothing really different with that myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T15:52:58-07:00","id":111805,"title":"","content":"Minor nomenclatural quibble, but it's bugging me:<br /> <br /> The two Slavic Courts are Sun and Moon, not Day and Night. I realize the latter sounds like it fits better between the Dawn and Dusk Courts, but that pair and the Slavic pair have nothing to do with each other. There is no published Day or Night Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T15:55:24-07:00","id":111808,"title":"","content":"Yea I call them Day and Night in my game and it is habitual. I will try and be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T04:01:09-07:00","id":111988,"title":"","content":"I have house ruled fan-based Contracts for the Sun/Day and Moon/Night; there were a couple versions kicking around the net before but there were a very big mixed bag, so they got revised further (The equivalents of &quot;Fleeting&quot; contracts for both need a further tweak though to dovetail more with Post-GMC Changeling house-rules present though). It helps make up for it, though post GMC has made more work on the roster to do some last revisions.<br /> <br /> I don't worry too much about the two courts nomenclature; it's pretty interchangeable in my games and everyone knows what's being referred to anyhow. As is, the cultural identity isn't really the focus of them regardless; it's symbolism that has some traditional use, but not as a given. Human culture does not set the tone nor the Courts important elements; it's a convenience in symbolism that gets borrowed, the undercurrent behind it. Otherwise you start falling into characters from culture X should be this court, and those from Y that court... not something I like to encourage even if the roots might have nods to that.<br /> <br /> Honestly, many of the &quot;Slavic&quot; elements in those two courts writeups really had more to do with much younger Christian revisions (and in at least one instance and outright deity fabrication to make it fit with that religious pov) than much honestly old Slavic anyhow, a personal pet peeve of mine. To be blunt the Dualistic approach is a very poor fit for a Slavic base regardless, so I make due without paying too heavy mind to it as a big thing.<br /> <br /> The Directional have some very, very under-powered fan presentations out on the web that I'm updating as needed (player interest basically). There aren't enough active PC wise to worry about it too much yet, so it's update-as-needed; I've mostly not worried about them for NPCs, and PC's going for the fan-made contracts will get updates and discussion as they decide to snag them (hasn't happened yet). They weren't around when I first started running C:tL and the current fan-made need a -lot- of work, luckily nobody has had an issue with that thus far and it hasn't been problematic (Nobody can really help that the Seasonal got all the love). The goal is to get them all tweaked and updated, but it's a lot of work when other areas have had higher priority. If the Southern Courtier player wants a Contract or two to play up their Court aspects, I'll revise it then.<br /> <br /> On the Courts in my main Chronicle ( very long, fair warning, but it may help give you more context Baron):<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> There is/was a Freehold dedicated to the Seasonal Courts with one lone Dusk Courtier that's fell into disarray with the remaining freehold members looking at building a new one to get from under some fairly draconian (if not near-insane) members. The Dusk Courtier originally being an agent of the Sun/Moon/Dusk Freehold elsewhere to keep it abreast of what was going on in the city proper. The Directional Courts have their own Freehold entrenched in the city's setting, and the smaller city that recently became a suburb plays host to the Day/Night/Dusk freehold across the settings major lake with the Dusk taking on a more mercenary role/neutral party between the two. Fatalism is a fairly common thing to crop up; they just ended up finding the greatest foothold among the Moon/Sun courts by fulfilling a handy role there.<br /> <br /> There are no Dawn around, nor are there likely to be in the near future without something drastic occurring. I've no real interest in them as an ST, nor is there from my Co-St for the main chronicle at this time. Hope is a very, very rare commodity and the Martyrs usually just don't survive for long. Most that are aware of them locally see them as little more than Gentry-bait and sacrificial lambs to keep everyone else safe and sure as hell don't want them supping at their table for long. Great to have when one needs a distraction, and encouraged for just as long as it takes for them to live up to being a Martyr and divert Gentry (and others) away from the rest of the community. That could change, but there hasn't been anything towards that yet.<br /> <br /> It's less a free-for-all and isn't focused around one Freehold. It's far more &quot;If you want to be this Court, these are the folks NPC-wise you've likely worked with and had contact with in the past. This is also likely which Freehold that took you in initially unless you switched Courts in your past.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cross Freehold interactions were fairly limited and sparse in the setting; nothing formal though individual private dealings weren't too rare, simply kept quiet.<br /> <br /> The Seasonal Freehold (The Fortean Times) was overtly over-paranoid to the point of hostility towards outsiders beyond the one Dusk and a Courtless due to some rather low Clarity and rather aggressive Court rulers. The Autumn Court and Winter Court consistently had the most numbers, influence and power. Now a lot of the younger members, especially those with a better grip on reality are getting fed up and trying to make something less isolationist, secretive and at times downright vicious (the paranoia of Privateers and Loyalists led the original freehold to take very, very unpleasant approaches to untrustworthy new Changelings). The last Summer Court among them is kind of the last catalyst; if he leaves there won't be a proper cycle even if the season runs short regionally, and he's looking at potentially leaving that court entirely for the Dusk or Winter Courtiers if things keep going the way they have.<br /> <br /> The second is the Directional (The 1000 Hells), with one Night Courtier who decided to live in the main city as a vassal to them in the central area to exist in the comfortably (and feed a bit back to the Night Court every now and then). They're fairly cosmopolitan in numbers compared to the prior, but -very- strict. They'll likely see more prominence as the strongest Seasonal Freehold finishes its troubled times. They relied more on the acquisition mundane power and the influence of humans than the old Seasonal Court and it allowed them to hide more readily in plain sight. They weren't the most potent, but they were the most stable. Now that the prior Freehold is starting to topple they're coming out of the woodwork more and more.<br /> <br /> The third were small band of primarily Moon/Sun (The Blasted Rock) with a smattering of Dusk and off-the-radar until the main city's &quot;acquisition&quot; of the nearby large town/small city started bringing the city's problems to their doorstep. They want more of a foothold in the main city districts and have been sending out feelers and agents to muster that more actively; whether they'll butt heads with the Directional is tough to say yet. For the most part they're more worried about their survival as a distinct, separate Freehold and so have been taking steps to get inroads or alliances more recently to keep their asses covered.<br /> <br /> It's a big city; the Freeholds tend to be rather insular with a tone set by a sort of informal policy where they didn't want the problems of another Freehold coming to their own door, with outright sabotage by other Freeholds at times due consistent issues with Loyalists and Privateers gutting newcomer Freeholds from within and without (an issue which really set the tone for the Seasonal and Directional Freeholds). The longest standing ones have seen others come and go time-line wise precisely for drawing too much attention to the Gentry or the ire of other more populous supernaturals by being too open, too trusting and too cosmopolitan in their interactions.<br /> <br /> Of course, the truth of the matter is uglier than even that but you won't generally hear the Directional nor original Seasonal Freehold admit that some of those toppled short-lived Freeholds had more to do with power-plays, infighting, insanity and pure misinformation (including to their own Court members on what was occurring). Like any governing bodies in practice they tend to be self-serving assholes when they think they can get ahead at the cost of others who don't follow their outlooks, even if it might impact their mutual survival. Duck, cover, entrench and stay out of each others way and spy when you can on the surface. Back-stab, sabotage, gathering of leverage and who's fucking who behind closed doors before you even get legitimate Loyalists and Privateers involved. Latent human nature plus the mix of very real looming bogeyman, mad gods and stranger all around doesn't make for them suddenly playing nice.<br /> <br /> Desperate times call for desperate measures (and that's why you see Dusk crop up frequently in the setting as an almost rogue element). There's a reason the Dusk, Winter and Autumn Court used crop up frequently or for the longest time had the most actual power under their belts. It's starting to switch gears however, with the Dusk, Spring and South seeing more activity in this chronicle lately. I wouldn't at all be surprised if the Summer Court start seeing a resurgence at some point (especially if the old Summer Courtier of the Fortean Times sees something to give him hope to fight back rather change courts), possibly even a lone Dawn later on if the tone more drastically shifts and some of the years-long real time plots resolve.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T10:16:44-07:00","id":112102,"title":"","content":"Past player Seemings, from memory (despite the fact that I still have all the sheets) and arranged by game:<br /> <br /> Beast (Runnerswift), Beast (Hunterheart), Elemental (Woodblood)<br /> <br /> Beast (Runnerswift), Darkling (Gravewight), Darkling (Palewraith), Elemental (Manikin), Fairest (Dancer), Ogre (Gristlegrinder), Wizened (Soldier)<br /> <br /> Beast (Broadback), Beast (Runnerswift), Darkling (Mirrorskin), Fairest (Flowering), Fairest (Bright One)<br /> <br /> Beast (Steepscrambler), Elemental (Fireheart), Elemental (Snowskin), Fairest (Dancer/Swimmerskin), Ogre (Witchtooth)<br /> <br /> Not included are a few oneshots that were kind of shitty, and so not very memorable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T09:05:31-07:00","id":112689,"title":"","content":"Ogre (Stonebones), Fairest (Treasured), Wizened (Chirugeon), Darkling (Antiquarian)<br /> <br /> Elemental (Mannikin), Fairest (Flamesiren), Wizened (Drudge), Ogre (Farwalker)<br /> <br /> Fairest (Bright One/Dancer), Darkling (Antiquarian), Wizened (Woodwalker), Beast (Skitterskulk)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.j